{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick","id":987592,"title":"Sex Magick?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T21:16:47-07:00","id":987592,"title":"Sex Magick?","content":"So, i was curious if anyone has ever used this on your MtA game. or do you try to avoid that area of the game? my player's been discussing about the idea of their PC's using Tantric Magick but they still have no idea for which exact purpose/ effect would they do so.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:58:18-07:00","id":987605,"title":"","content":"Well...for the purpose, you must remember that doing the horizontal mambo is not an Instrument you can use on the fly. It is not possible to stop in the middle of a gunfight to do anything sexual. Or at least not terribly appropriate or wise. So it's probably best used for ritual and preparation work.<br /> <br /> This would also serve to alleviate some of the uncomfortable elements of sex magick. When the character is between missions or whatever, they can just tell the Storyteller that they go spend time with the significant other(s). Or alone, as the case may be. Arete is rolled, Effects are tallied, and the table moves on. No need to get into the details, given that the actual acts are straightforward enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T04:46:52-07:00","id":987705,"title":"","content":"Casting beneficial Mind effects (Not only Mind 1 - everything up to and including Mind 5) on herself or another person could be done with sex.<br /> For Correspondence, a previous lover could be reached or effected. With Time 4 hanging, a future lover could be effected.<br /> Divinations seem a natural fit for sex, seeing it can be treated as a form of a trance. One could perhaps feel and talk out the details of the vision with their partner; divining could involve another practice in this case. (Like a steamy bath or a visit to a sauna.)<br /> Prime &amp; sex seem a pairing as well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987605#post987605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...for the purpose, you must remember that doing the horizontal mambo is not an Instrument you can use on the fly. It is not possible to stop in the middle of a gunfight to do anything sexual. Or at least not terribly appropriate or wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you are a Son of the Ether who has harnessed the power of the orgasm. When vulgar effects are called for in the field, he can use his gear to induce one. (Either by direct stimulation, or with a device that records and compresses a sexual encounter, and flashes it into his mind.)<br /> (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orgone\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orgone</a>)<br /> <br /> <br /> An Ecstatic rote:<br /> <b>The Flames of Love</b> Time 4, Forces 3 or 5, Prime 2<br /> The idea about this rote is simple - it stores the heat of passion of a sexual encounter, and releases it in the form of a Forces 3 fireball later. The effect can be triggered in various ways - one Cultist says a word that hanged in their memory during the act; another might cast the rote with lewd gestures. There are also those that share a box of Mercis (or other chocolates) with their lover, while leaving one sweet out of the box to be eaten as an anchor for the rote. Of course the most appropriate is casting the rote with the last cigarette out of a pack, and a matching lighter. (Though some have discovered, if time is short, the cigarette lights itself as part of the rote.)<br /> <br /> To conjure a Forces 5 inferno, an Ecastic Master of Forces must organize an intricate orgy. As an anchor to store it one could for example bake a cake together and leave a single piece for later; or play a single piece of music (or music of the same artist) throughout the orgy, and put it on later. Recitation of the names of those that took part can also work. Cigarettes work as well, though a few have to be smoked in succession. (The cigarettes need to match the kinds that were smoked by the participants.)<br /> <br /> <b>The Flames of Love</b> can be cast from the passion of casual sex.<br /> It has been a source of much speculation and experimentation whether other elements can be conjured with sex. There are rumors of some Ecstatics naturally creating ice instead of fire - though this might just be jibes towards them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-15-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T05:37:15-07:00","id":987709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987705#post987705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could perhaps feel and talk out the details of the vision with their partner;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want you to visualize two or more people having sex and one of them suddenly begins recounting visions without ruining the mood entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:08:10-07:00","id":987716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987709#post987709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I want you to visualize two or more people having sex and one of them suddenly begins recounting visions without ruining the mood entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can visualize them doing this after sex. :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:37:24-07:00","id":987722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick#post987592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, i was curious if anyone has ever used this on your MtA game. or do you try to avoid that area of the game? my player's been discussing about the idea of their PC's using Tantric Magick but they still have no idea for which exact purpose/ effect would they do so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of my games had it. The Verbena's was used primarily for life-giving and life-taking. It was about the connection between two living beings, the energies at play. My witch has, among other things, used sex to commune with the divine, to harmonize with the populace, to imbue herself and others, to curse, to empower massive rites.<br /> <br /> Almost as often she'd use sex magick without being directly involved - other creatures or people engaged in the act is more than enough if the magick is about them or their impact on the place. This one time she helped organize an enormous, often orgiastic party, and used that as a battery to bless an entire &quot;feud&quot; with bountiful harvests.<br /> <br /> Things revolving around sex would come at play a lot for more subtle effects too. Sexuality is something a tantric mage quite literally exhudes. It's hard to <b>not</b> think about how useful it can be for social magick. A ridiculously easy one is distracting people or getting them to act impulsively just for being flustered by your insinuations. Even if your insinuation was barely more than moving just so and so while, dunno, asking the salesman about the specs of a motorcycle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:20:56-07:00","id":987734,"title":"","content":"You could probably use Sex as a focus for Fusion type Life effects.In this way the two (or more) involved are literally becoming one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> How do you roleplay the Sex part of the effect without things becoming either awkward or a stream of sex jokes from the other players?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:10:13-07:00","id":987755,"title":"","content":"One of my players is infiltrating a the ennemy at the moment. She uses sex magick to enter his dreams, know his plans and alter his mind to make him her puppet. So yes, it's been done in my game and it's pretty fun. Using sex as an instrument is possible with all sort of magick. Mind magick may be the easiest. But Life is possible too and of course Time (The Time 3 / Mind 3 &quot;Longest orgasm ever&quot; can be a useful tool to get information when you play the Mata Hari kind of Mage ^^).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:21:11-07:00","id":987812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987734#post987734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably use Sex as a focus for Fusion type Life effects.In this way the two (or more) involved are literally becoming one.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar32_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"32\" data-vbnamecard=\"32\">Synapse</a> How do you roleplay the Sex part of the effect without things becoming either awkward or a stream of sex jokes from the other players?</div> </div> </div> </div>While my groups tend to be moronically silly, we really enjoy the ambience and the evocativeness of magick, such rituals are respeceted during game time.<br /> It's rare for them to be confortable with more graphic narratives. The baseline usually goes the Tell Don't Show way. Everyone pictures the details how they want.<br /> <br /> There is potential for trollish hilarity if your mate is also playing and has a similar paradigm. Oh the imagery we invoked and enacted just to see how faar they'd let us XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 10-15-2016, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:56:33-07:00","id":987835,"title":"","content":"Sex magic is often more useful for Sorcerers than Mages, because Sorcerers tend to have to use long rituals to create their more impressive effects anyway. Like most things involving sex, it is generally more fun to do it than to talk about it, and I have found that the majority of players only need one session with sex magic being in the forefront to get bored with it. It can be fun when you have a few couples playing, though people can get strangely jealous when their lover's PC gets sexual with someone other than their PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:44:09-07:00","id":987945,"title":"","content":"Long ritual work isn't limited to Sorcerers. It's more or less required for them, but that's a subtle distinction. Mages have their fair share of long ritual work, simply by virtue of sharing the same metaphysical systems as their unAwakened counterparts. A Hermetic, for instance, has to spend many minutes - or sometimes hours or days - in protracted bouts of chanting inside a candle-lit circle, regardless of whether they use static or dynamic magic.<br /> <br /> To address @Maud'Dib, I don't even know if the Time 4 element of that ritual is strictly necessary, though you could still do it. Mage: The Ascension has pointed out here and there that many Mages do a lot of prep-work beforehand, so they can enjoy the fruits of that labor on the fly later on. The aforementioned Hermetic might perform a long series of chants in a circle, directing their energies to the planet Mars or whatever, but refrain from speaking the last word until it is needed. Or he'll use a similar ceremony to ritually carve a wand with the secret names of the archangel of fire, that can be used as an Instrument. The main advantages of using Time 4 (or Prime 2/3, in the case of Charms) is being able to roll Arete well in advance, which gives the Mage more time to compensate if the roll ends in failure. That, and because the exact moment of the Effect going off can be arranged.<br /> <br /> As such, it makes perfect sense for a sex magician to use prior fun times as prep work for later magicks. Obviously, no one can be expected to hold off on the &quot;big finish&quot; for several hours. But one might save the after-copulation cigarette for later (an act that also brings the power of self-denial into the mix, as the Mage probably wants to smoke at any point between the bedroom blitz and whenever they use the magick). Or the Mage refuses to wash after the encounter, so they retain a strong musk. Scent is, after all, one of the most influential yet unnoticed senses for humans. Or, if the Mage is &quot;lonely&quot;, they can use a sex toy, charging it with &quot;sexual energy&quot;, that can then be carried and employed later.<br /> <br /> Granted, this does mean a Mage game has the potential to see a PC beating someone over the head with a dildo. I'll leave the decision over whether this is bad or good up to the reader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:55:57-07:00","id":988289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987945#post987945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long ritual work isn't limited to Sorcerers. It's more or less required for them, but that's a subtle distinction. Mages have their fair share of long ritual work, simply by virtue of sharing the same metaphysical systems as their unAwakened counterparts. A Hermetic, for instance, has to spend many minutes - or sometimes hours or days - in protracted bouts of chanting inside a candle-lit circle, regardless of whether they use static or dynamic magic.<br /> <br /> To address @Maud'Dib, I don't even know if the Time 4 element of that ritual is strictly necessary, though you could still do it. Mage: The Ascension has pointed out here and there that many Mages do a lot of prep-work beforehand, so they can enjoy the fruits of that labor on the fly later on. The aforementioned Hermetic might perform a long series of chants in a circle, directing their energies to the planet Mars or whatever, but refrain from speaking the last word until it is needed. Or he'll use a similar ceremony to ritually carve a wand with the secret names of the archangel of fire, that can be used as an Instrument. The main advantages of using Time 4 (or Prime 2/3, in the case of Charms) is being able to roll Arete well in advance, which gives the Mage more time to compensate if the roll ends in failure. That, and because the exact moment of the Effect going off can be arranged.<br /> <br /> As such, it makes perfect sense for a sex magician to use prior fun times as prep work for later magicks. Obviously, no one can be expected to hold off on the &quot;big finish&quot; for several hours. But one might save the after-copulation cigarette for later (an act that also brings the power of self-denial into the mix, as the Mage probably wants to smoke at any point between the bedroom blitz and whenever they use the magick). Or the Mage refuses to wash after the encounter, so they retain a strong musk. Scent is, after all, one of the most influential yet unnoticed senses for humans. Or, if the Mage is &quot;lonely&quot;, they can use a sex toy, charging it with &quot;sexual energy&quot;, that can then be carried and employed later.<br /> <br /> Granted, this does mean a Mage game has the potential to see a PC beating someone over the head with a dildo. I'll leave the decision over whether this is bad or good up to the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>All this sounds EXACTLY how Time 4 works. That's a key problem with the power hierarchy in Mage magic. The idea of the &quot;missing piece completion&quot; spell isn't actually possible unless a character has heavily invested in a Sphere that might not otherwise be appropriate or in character. At all. And &quot;missing piece completion&quot; magic is all the rage in fantasy fiction, for all sorts of mages who AREN'T seers or scryers or diviners. (Actually it seems most common with &quot;blast mages&quot;.) <br /> <br /> If you don't want to have to wait for Arete 4 and slog your way through to Time 4 (if that's not your thing), the rules leave you with a couple of options. Get Prime and make some Charms. That definitely mimic some of the ideas discussed above. Otherwise, sex does seem like a great way to set up continuing effects with successes dumped into duration that don't just &quot;come into effect&quot; like some kind of orgasm aftershock but more as a continuous post-coital afterglow sort of thing. Whether it makes you bulletproof, let's you see around corners, puts you into a state of &quot;bar time&quot; like prescience or just makes you just centered enough to keep people from getting easy access to your mind. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T11:22:10-07:00","id":988310,"title":"","content":"An important distinction:<br /> 1. \u201cmissing piece completion\u201c as a instrument (in particular High Ritual practicioners)<br /> 2. \u201cmissing piece completion\u201c as a trigger for Time 4<br /> <br /> In the first case Arete is rolled in the field, probably under bad conditions and against the clock.<br /> In the second case Arete rolling is already over, probably under good conditions and if you utter the final word the target(s) get zapped with a boatload of successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:53:28-07:00","id":988421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=988310#post988310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important distinction:<br /> 1. \u201cmissing piece completion\u201c as a instrument (in particular High Ritual practicioners)<br /> 2. \u201cmissing piece completion\u201c as a trigger for Time 4<br /> <br /> In the first case Arete is rolled in the field, probably under bad conditions and against the clock.<br /> In the second case Arete rolling is already over, probably under good conditions and if you utter the final word the target(s) get zapped with a boatload of successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, no. The whole missing piece as completion for an instrument is a dodge that really doesn't work with regard to the rest of the rules. If you allow it, then no one needs Time 4 to do the whole &quot;keep the spell in your back pocket&quot; thing and people are <i><u><b>adamant </b></u></i>about the Time Trigger has to be Time 4 thing. The two ideas are antithetical. You need to do the whole ritual on the fly, short form, ripping through it and probably blitzing it. AKA &quot;Fast-Casting&quot;. Otherwise, what you are saying is, effectively, &quot;The Instrument (high ritual) is needed, except it's not, because ritual as an Instrument doesn't really mean anything at all that squares with any concept of &quot;ritual&quot;, including those explicitly set out in RAW.&quot; <br /> <br /> Or.... just get rid of the damn Time Trigger Time 4 necessity and let people do the &quot;hang the spell with the last word or whatever left and then BOOM&quot; thing and have Time 4 do something else.... like, say, sending the effect through time to the moment when it's needed. (Which does mean that Time Adepts probably would line up a lot of scrying and then sending effects through time when they were safe and cozy.. but... well.... doesn't that seem like something an Adept could do to some degree or another?) <br /> <br /> But it's a significant kink in the rules that doesn't get resolved, even though it could be, and fairly easily too, because of rules inertia, like so much else in Mage where &quot;streamlined&quot; open-ended rules are a actually a streamlined set of rules embedded in a mess of sloppy, tangled idiosyncrasies in a state of perpetual conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:59:14-07:00","id":988522,"title":"","content":"Time 4 is useful for more than just replicating what a Mage could do with Instruments. It's magick set on a timer. Without Time 4, the Mage is dependent on being able to use their tools at the time they need it. Time 4 turns the use of that Effect into an inevitability.<br /> <br /> It's like that bit from Watchmen. &quot;Do you seriously think I'd explain my master-stroke if there remained the slightest chance of you affecting its outcome? I did it thirty-five minutes ago.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not even killing the Mage who cast the Effect will stop it, because it's in Time's hands now. Indeed, adding Life to the Time 4 could hang the results of the Effect on the Mage's death. The ultimate insurance policy. Matter could be used to tie the Effect on an item (much like a Charm, but without the Tass requirements), which could conceivably be used by anyone who knows how to set it off. Entropy 3 could make the Effect go off if a certain event occurs, like true love's kiss or the election of a certain person to President. And with enough successes, the hung Effect could even be made to re-occur over several generations.<br /> <br /> Yes, there is overlap between what Time 4 can do, and what a Mage can do as part of their Focus. But the advantages of the Focus-based method are severely limited. In another sense, a person who performs a ritual and then speaks the last word when they need it isn't doing anything mechanically different than the Etherite who builds a machine with Science(!) and then pushes a button. Or the Fae-blooded Mage who writes a contract with the elements, and later states in clear language that they call upon a clause of said contract.<br /> <br /> All of these things are groundwork. If you must insist on RAW, then the Instrument these characters use is merely what they employ or have at the moment they need it. The High Ritualist's Instrument is a single word, the Etherite's is a button press on the machine, and the Fae-blooded Mage's is the declaration of having a contract and calling it in. Everything else is roleplaying and character stuff.<br /> <br /> Time 4, as demonstrated here and elsewhere, is significantly more flexible, and capable of going above and beyond what is possible otherwise. I don't think any Mage could have an Effect of their's go off after they've died, without Time 4. Let alone <i>centuries</i> after they died. That's kind of the point of this part of the Time Sphere, and why it requires such a high rank.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-16-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:20:17-07:00","id":988591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987709#post987709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I want you to visualize two or more people having sex and one of them suddenly begins recounting visions without ruining the mood entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you're doing it right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One good reference point I could recommend for Cult of Ecstasy, specifically the use of sex magic to achieve Time effects, is <i>Sex Criminals</i> by Matt Fraction and Chip Zdarsky. Warning up front: as one might guess it has explicit adult content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:31:17-07:00","id":988949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=988522#post988522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of these things are groundwork. If you must insist on RAW, then the Instrument these characters use is merely what they employ or have at the moment they need it. The High Ritualist's Instrument is a single word, the Etherite's is a button press on the machine, and the Fae-blooded Mage's is the declaration of having a contract and calling it in. Everything else is roleplaying and character stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Sorry. The High Ritualist's Instrument is the entire ritual. The Etherites is both the gadget and the invention of same. (That's why Etherites REALLY need to take Prime in RAW). The fae-blooded mage... well, that's not really so much of a thing. It's nice to think that the rules allow for the &quot;hanging spell&quot; but they have clearly and definitively stated that hanging spells is ONLY allowed with Time 4. Period. End of story. It's been addressed to the developers and hashed and re-hashed over an over again and the party line belies what you are saying. <br /> <br /> I don't agree with it. But then I don't agree with the bollixed up mess of near uselessness that is the wreck of the Time Sphere overall. No clear power progression. No parallelism with the other Spheres in line with the progression of power as laid out, etc. But there it is.<br /> <br /> I do like all those things you say Time 4 Time Trigger CAN do that isn't hanging spells. That's the sort of thing that Time should be able to do, but it's not. It's just a grab bag of things that look like the fit together but don't. I'm sure you could come up with a way to have a spell go off post-mortem without Time 4 as you describe, but Time 4 would make things so simple and elegant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:01:33-07:00","id":988988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=988949#post988949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Sorry. The High Ritualist's Instrument is the entire ritual. The Etherites is both the gadget and the invention of same. (That's why Etherites REALLY need to take Prime in RAW). The fae-blooded mage... well, that's not really so much of a thing. It's nice to think that the rules allow for the &quot;hanging spell&quot; but they have clearly and definitively stated that hanging spells is ONLY allowed with Time 4. Period. End of story. It's been addressed to the developers and hashed and re-hashed over an over again and the party line belies what you are saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, when published material directly supports my case. Or, rather, is the reason I argue it to begin with.<br /> <br /> From <i>Tradition Book: Order of Hermes Revised</i>, p. 64:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prep Time</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermetic foci, especially those for powerful or far-reaching Effects, entail the use of hours-long chants, elaborate preparations (ritual, alchemical or otherwise) and lengthy supplications to astral entities, just to name a few. In the thick of battle (or even just while having a coffee with friends at the local donut shop), one can't really afford to call &quot;time-out&quot; to inscribe six pentacles and mete out a single dram of mercury for each while issuing three pages of commands in Enochian to nearby elemental spirits.<br /> &quot;But wait,&quot; you say, &quot;this isn't fair!&quot;<br /> After all, an Akashic Brother can use her Do as a focus for her magic, even as she uses it as a focus for beating ass. Likewise, a Son of Ether merely needs to produce a bizarre particle beam weapon in order to channel his Forces 3, Prime 2 offensive Effect. True enough. However, the Akashic also needs to spend an hour or more each day centering herself through meditative states, various kata and the contemplation of sacred and philosophical texts. Similarly, the Son of Ether must actually build his foci, no matter how outlandish or how difficult that might be. <b>In the same way, a Hermetic mage can do her prep time at home or in the Sanctum, finishing all but the very last steps of her incantations, alchemical formulae and ritual gestures.</b> The guy on the wrong end of the wand won't care that it was cut from an oak split by lightning, hardened over white hot iron ingots and carved with the Ten Secret Names of Gabriel, but he will notice the results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice how nothing it that passage says anything about needing Time 4 to accomplish any of that. You can just do it. And it's not like the Mage gains an unfair advantage doing this. Those three Mages all need to spend a great deal of their time setting up for future rewards.<br /> <br /> Moreover, mandating that a Hermetic must have Time 4 to perform ritual preparations, or that an Etherite must know Prime 3+ in order to turn their every machine into a Device, is massively unfair to players who want to play either of those groups. The entire point of Mage: The Ascension is that, despite the different trappings, all Mages perform Magick in a mechanically identical manner. It's for this reason also that Magick is rolled from a separate magic Trait, rather than from Intelligence or something. To do otherwise would be to punish specific character types over others.<br /> <br /> Technical inconsistencies aside, the Storyteller System is about narrative and fun. When you start loading Mage down with additional Sphere requirements because of this or that reasoning, you get <i>How Do You Do That?</i>. And I think we can all agree that a lot of additions made in that book subtract from the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-17-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T13:49:25-07:00","id":989005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=988949#post988949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with it. But then I don't agree with the bollixed up mess of near uselessness that is the wreck of the Time Sphere overall. No clear power progression. No parallelism with the other Spheres in line with the progression of power as laid out, etc. But there it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, we're having one of those discussions I see...<br /> <br /> Time 1: Like all spheres, Time 1 is a sensory sphere. It allows you a perfect an intuitive understanding of time and the effects of time manipulation. You can tell what time it is with perfect accuracy no matter where you are. You can also feel how long something has taken or if you're familiar enough with the process, how long it will take. You can do multiple complex things at once staggered and rest assured you will never miss a single step. You can move in perfect time, keeping a steady beat or a proper frequency up longer than humanly possible without need of reference. Also, Time 1 can be combined with so many other spheres to make effects that last for exactly how long you want them to, or change every hour, every minute, or every day. Time 1 is so very underappreciated.<br /> This is on top of being able to sense the Time stream itself, which means being aware of any Time 4 effects in the area (big deal to avoid nasty surprises), sensing anyone scrying on you from across time, on interlopers from other times, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Time 2: Time sense. Just like Corr. 2 allows you to scry through space, Time 2 allows you to scry through time. This makes Time 2 one of the most amazing second level spheres in the game. You can look at possible events as well as past events, and the standard chart gives you a huge range to look through. You can use Time 2 to solve mysteries simply by rewatching the crime as it comes to pass. You can hear the last words of dying mages straight from the horses mouth. You can follow kidnappers who left long ago, allowing their &quot;time shadows&quot; to lead you right to their base. Similarly you can look into the future and be prepared for all kinds of nasty surprises and eventuality. Time 2 has the potential for being the single most Chronicle breaking sphere in the game if it isn't handled correctly. It's gloriously powerful. Combined with other spheres and you can read the minds of the past, see all possible destinies laid out before you, learn how long one has before they die, see exactly what a book looked like in the past (so if the words have faded, that's not a problem, you can read it as though it were newly printed).<br /> <br /> Time 3: Like all 3rd level spheres, you're able to start manipulating Time in much more obvious ways, this is where you get to start really messing around with the Time stream. Time 3 allows you to speed up and slow down events that play out around you. This could be just speeding yourself up, allowing several moves per action without penalty, or slowing your opponents down so you get the same benefit. It could also mean slowing down objects as they drop or speeding up cars as they travel. In the most extreme cases, you could even make a room which is 7x faster on the inside. (1 week inside is 1 day outside), allowing for weeks worth of research/preparation/invention/what have you, to be done without it causing delays in the real world. Heck, taken to the extreme, you could probably fit a whole day into an hour, allowing for days of practice and preparation to pass in the span of an afternoon. Combined with other spheres, you could speed up your own mental processes, slow down your own fate, speed up your own natural healing process (a clever way to heal Agg damage without needing Quintessence).<br /> And that's not even mentioning the best feature of Time 3. Time looping! The single most headache causing mechanic in the game! Just fell into a trap causing you 5 points of lethal? Nope! undone. Got ambushed by someone? Nope, Undo it and run! Oh no, that guy killed my friend! Nope! Undone, quick now prevent it! Looping time is one of my favourite aspects of Time 3, and if it weren't so heavily regulated, it would destroy a session before it even starts.<br /> if you<br /> <br /> Time 4: Pretty standard progression here. Time 1 lets you feel time, Time 2 lets you see through it, Time 3 lets you warp it. Now time 4 lets you twist time entirely! You can do the whole &quot;programmed events&quot; thing that's been talked about to death already. But you can also do that with normal things as well. You can pause people, things, events, places, or whatever! You can make explosions stop exploding and move them elsewhere. You can get people to freeze in place, monsters to stop, great cataclysmic events to halt, all in the aid of time. If a crystal vase about to fall and shatter? Time 4 it before it hits the ground, then pick it up and put it back. Is your friend about to die ? Freeze em and fix them with more time to deal with things. Oh no! That portal in the umbra is about to close! Quick! Time 4 it so we can run through it first! Time 4 is everything you want a high level sphere to be! It's so simple, and yet so wonderfully potent!<br /> <br /> Time 5: The best goddamn Master level sphere in the game! Yes you get Time Travel and all the trappings that come with it. Jump around changing things, undoing mistakes or making sure things go different, getting wisdom for the future, even casting spells directly through time into the past or future. Everything you'd expect, and yeah it's fun and all, but it pails in comparison to Time 5's other amazing trick. Time Immunity. It's glorious! You just stop time. You can do whatever the heck you want after that. Take your gun, walk up to them and shoot 5 or 6 times in the chest. Walk right through a chantry's defences and steal whatever you want without ever being stopped. Stop someone from making an escape just by casually searching for them and then tie them up. With Time 5, you are untouchable, and no one can do a thing to you. You always get the last word, and if you're ever surrounded or in any danger, just sidestep time and walk away.<br /> Best part is that there's nothing the other party can do about this, they won't even know this is happening...unless they have one thing, you know what that is?<br /> TIME 1! Heck yeah that's necessary!<br /> <br /> If you imagine Time as a stream, then 1 lets you dip your toes in Time, 2 lets you drink from the stream of Time, 3 lets you narrow or widen the banks of the stream and cause eddies in the flow. 4 allows you to move the stream around, making it bend to avoid certain things or places. 5 lets you disconnect from the direction of the flow entirely, allowing you to walk upon the water, standing over its frozen surface either to explore new parts or simply move things around before the stream unfreezes.<br /> <br /> That's how the progression works, and it is beautiful!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-17-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T14:20:59-07:00","id":989016,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I think we can all agree that the ability to go full <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Y6Aevo-XvsA?t=39s\" target=\"_blank\">Dio Brando</a> is worth the price of admission. And if you can't think of something useful to do with the previous ranks in Time, I don't know what to tell you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:46:18-07:00","id":989469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=989016#post989016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, I think we can all agree that the ability to go full <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Y6Aevo-XvsA?t=39s\" target=\"_blank\">Dio Brando</a> is worth the price of admission. And if you can't think of something useful to do with the previous ranks in Time, I don't know what to tell you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the problem. Any decent player can do cool things with what they are given. People can do cool things with Entropy and that Sphere is complete garbage in every way. (In fact, Time is a much more workable Sphere if all the non-duplicated stuff from Entropy is ported over).<br /> <br /> There is a way Spheres are supposed to work. It's in the rules (M20 that is). BEFORE any Spheres are detailed. Time and Entropy don't work that way. Mind is a prime offender at Mind 1. The outline is clearly set out and then promptly ignored. Mostly due to rules inertia and pretty much nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:04:38-07:00","id":989478,"title":"","content":"And there he is, still calling things garbage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No, Entropy is not complete garbage in every way, may be you just have trouble playing with it, which is fine but does not really allow you to put it to trash. My players have a nice time with it and they like it a lot, as I do and as a lot of people do too. As you said it, poeple can do cool things with it, so it should be enough, don't you think ?<br /> <br /> And there is no way that Spheres are <i>supposed</i> to work. Talks like a pure Hermetic that one ^^... Spheres are just the way there are to build a game-system that is here to help create good stories. They are not an end, just a means, and there is nothing good nor wrong with it. If you do not like it, then do not play with it and make up your own system. Many poeple make houserules when they're not satisfied with the system, I do it myself quite often when it serves the story. The system is not flawless and it should no be (nothing is nor should be perfect, praise Chaos \\o/). I get that it does not satisfy some poeple and the only advise I can give is that above all rules, there is the Golden Rule, which is pretty clear: you can do everything you want.<br /> <br /> And conerning the global (and I mean global, not completely exact) functioning of the Spheres, I think that all Spheres are rather consistent, including Time, Entropy, and Mind. I'm not sure that the point of this thread was to digress on that topic though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T18:13:13-07:00","id":989641,"title":"","content":"Also, none of the spheres really fit into a common progression.<br /> <br /> Corr. goes: Sense space, see through space, put your whole body through space, put space through space, destroy all notion of space.<br /> <br /> Entropy goes: Sense fate/chance, alter random chance/fate [win at cards], alter repeatable/mechanical events [win at vending machines], alter dynamic/organic events [win at genetics], alter complicated/memetic events [win at the internet].<br /> <br /> Forces goes: Sense energy [It's hot], change small [now it's cold], transform small [now it's lightning?], change big [Now that's a big storm!], transform big [The storm is now gravity, goodbye physics].<br /> <br /> Life goes: Sense life [Bob], change small/self [bob with healthy plants], transform small/self change big/other [Bob with wings], polymorph self/small transform big/other [Bob gives you wings (and subsequently gets a job at Red Bull], Become new self/small polymorph big/other [Bob is a red bull]<br /> <br /> Matter goes: Sense matter [it's a wall] , Change what it's made off [a wall of butter], change what it's shape is (simple) [the butter is now air!], change what it's shape is (complex) change what it's made of (complex) [this air butter turns into spray on toast], ignore physics [the spray on toast is delicious].<br /> <br /> Mind goes: Sense emotion [^_^], sense thought change emotion [0_0], sense memory change thought [&gt;_&lt;], change memory become thought (astral project) []-_- , create mind, [@_@]<br /> <br /> Prime goes: I see shiny! Make me Shiny! I'll make you Shiny! I'll make your stuff Shiny! Everything is Shiny!<br /> <br /> Spirit goes: Sense spirit, say hi to spirit, come round to visit spirit, force spirit to visit in return, create new spirit who will appreciate you for you.<br /> <br /> Time: it's 5:00pm right now, I can see 6:00pm right now, It will be 7:00pm in a few minutes, you'll completely miss 8:00pm, It is 9:00am right now.<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> I spent way more time on this than I should have...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-18-2016, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:37:25-07:00","id":990192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=989478#post989478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there he is, still calling things garbage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No, Entropy is not complete garbage in every way, may be you just have trouble playing with it, which is fine but does not really allow you to put it to trash. My players have a nice time with it and they like it a lot, as I do and as a lot of people do too. As you said it, poeple can do cool things with it, so it should be enough, don't you think ?<br /> <br /> And there is no way that Spheres are <i>supposed</i> to work. Talks like a pure Hermetic that one ^^... Spheres are just the way there are to build a game-system that is here to help create good stories. They are not an end, just a means, and there is nothing good nor wrong with it. If you do not like it, then do not play with it and make up your own system. Many poeple make houserules when they're not satisfied with the system, I do it myself quite often when it serves the story. The system is not flawless and it should no be (nothing is nor should be perfect, praise Chaos \\o/). I get that it does not satisfy some poeple and the only advise I can give is that above all rules, there is the Golden Rule, which is pretty clear: you can do everything you wa<br /> And conerning the global (and I mean global, not completely exact) functioning of the Spheres, I think that all Spheres are rather consistent, including Time, Entropy, and Mind. I'm not sure that the point of this thread was to digress on that topic though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, stop making statements about which you have no knowledge. I have played characters with Entropy VERY effectively. I have played even more NPCs with Entropy just as well, if not better. It's not hard to play the Sphere. That doesn't make it good game design. It's not hard to play even crap rules very effectively. Sometimes even more effectively when they are crap. (Anyone remember the D&amp;D spell <i>sepia snake sigil</i>?) Not in this case however. Almost everything in Entropy is actually already handled elsewhere (Matter, Life, Time, Mind, etc.). And handled better.<br /> <br /> It's a crap Sphere. It doesn't even need to exist from a rules standpoint. (Though there may be a little slip of something there.) There's no there there (to misquote Gertrude Stein) There is a reason why Entropy was split up when Awakening was created.<br /> <br /> Ummmm.... there is a way Spheres are supposed to work. It's right there. In the rules. There is supposed to be a clear progression of power. Game design is supposed to be parity between Spheres. No Sphere should be clearly unequivocally better than another at any particular level. By that, I mean the Sphere on it's face. Not when it is tortured and twisted until it screams or crossed with 1-8 other Spheres to enact. This isn't about your game or my game or anyone else's particular game an the specific choices that are made to keep the game fluid and fun. It's about the core rules. <br /> <br /> And I take the idea of being a Hermetic. But I'm more likely N.W.O. <br /> <br /> The reason why we seem to have tangented off this direction is the whole concept of &quot;holding on to your orgasm&quot; and using it to light a cigarette (or a bonfire) later. Which led to a discussion of spell triggers. Which inevitably leads to a discussion of Time. Which segues to the overall &quot;(Dis)harmony of the Spheres&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 10-19-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T20:04:09-07:00","id":990224,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1062_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1062\" data-vbnamecard=\"1062\">Ajax</a> <br /> \u200bEntropy is actually pretty nifty if you're inventive enough. While the other spheres focus on getting specific things to occur, Entropy works the other way around. It controls the outcome of events, but not the events themselves. This makes it one of the single most subtle spheres in the game. It's also the ultimate sphere of &quot;you can't tie that to me, it just happened&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the things it affects actually can't be done with other spheres.<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 allows you to sense events, importance, fortune, and how much chaos there is in any given thing. No other sphere can do this. No other sphere can help you find something specific without knowing what it is first. If you're looking for a sacred idol, sure you could use Matter or Corr to search for it manually, or you could use Entropy to know exactly which box is more important than all the others because it has your sacred idol in it. Job done!<br /> <br /> Also, if you're planning an escape route, Entropy 1 makes you basically not have to worry about stealth. You can sense out where the right place to be is and the right path to go down. No need to mind magic yourself easy to ignore or Forces yourself as invisible, you can just get away by knowing where to be and not to be. No other sphere can do that.<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 is all about makes things happen the way you want them to. You want the perfect hand in a poker game? Boom, you have it. You want the traffic lights to change just after you cross them, slowing down your pursuer? Boom, it is done, and no petty fiddling around with Forces, Corr to target, and Technology rolls to know if you have the knowledge required to know where to put the Force power to change the lights manually. You need to meet people in a crowd without having to find them? Look who you just bumped into! Oh, but what if you don't want to get found? Well, I'll just decrease the chance of my pursuer coming anywhere near me. Nice! It's all coincidental, you don't have to target anyone (meaning no Corr requirement or proximity to target). Uh oh, I lost my talisman! Let's just Entropy 2 it so I just happen to find it in the first place I look. This is your basic &quot;Get Stuff Done&quot; sphere, no other 2nd level sphere grants you this.<br /> <br /> Entropy 3. Now we're getting into the cool stuff. Anything predictable is under your purview. Make machines work better or stop working being the most obvious one. It sounds drab when you put it like that. But think about it. There's a security camera up there, Boom, All it can see is static, no need to break it with Forces. Coincidental and Innocent. Just what you want for stealth. Quick we have to get away! But all we have is this rickety old car! hmm. Either I could try to fix it up mundanely with some Matter assistance, or I could just Entropy it to work well enough while I need it. Which one do you think is going to take less time? (read fewer successes, less need of an extended ritual, and requires a 3 dot sphere rather than a 4 dot sphere to do efficiently)<br /> <br /> However, this can also be applied to predictable processes, so computer programs that run on a schedule, you can totally cause that schedule to donk up, meaning suddenly the entire office's computer system is locked out due to &quot;scheduled&quot; maintenance, The perfect way to delay your Technocrats. Cause guns to misfire while they're in their holsters, get walls to collapse with exactly the right hit. Or do the opposite, make your walls uncannily strong, have your guns fire so well and so precisely it is literally impossible to botch with them. Make your phone work even if it's been plunged into the ocean. So subtle but so very effective. Entropy you beast!<br /> <br /> Entropy 4. Life is Dynamic, it kinda does what it wants. All you can do with Life magic is say what you want it to do and try to guide it down that route. Entropy, on the other hand, lets you control the outcome (and leave the life pattern to get on with it on its own). You want to get rid of disease? Bam, done. You want to give someone a disease? They be sick! You want someones skin to just start pealing off? Off it goes! You want to look great? Bam, you do. You want the garden to grow beautifully? Bam it's there. With Life magic you'd have to control each and every single thing directly, and chances are it'll be vulgar as hell. Not Entropy 4 though. It gets stuff done, and no need to multi sphere to do it!<br /> <br /> Entropy 5. This is where things get scary. You basically control people and events as though they were a hive mind. You can make everyone decide to put up their umbrellas at exactly the right time to hide beneath them. You could manipulate ideas so that they just happen to come up at the opportune time. You can basically inception the Mind mage without them ever knowing what you've done. Oh yeah, you can also just straight up rewrite peoples fates. Damn that's powerful. Sorry, I don't feel like being a martyr today, I'll just make it so John is the martyr now. Good luck John!<br /> <br /> That's the other big thing about Entropy. It's the get stuff done sphere that lets you touch a whole host of things that, for any other sphere, you'd need other spheres to do. With Entropy 5, you don't need Mind, Matter, Forces, or Life to still affect the outcome of these things. Talk about sphere economy! No other sphere allows this level of fluidity. This also means getting around wards and blocks made with other spheres, which can always grant on the edge.<br /> <br /> Mixed with other spheres, you can reek all kinds of havoc that can't be done without Entropy.<br /> <br /> 1 for sensing weak areas in structures, feeling out cracks in the gauntlet, knowing where or when important things are going to happen.<br /> 2 for randomising your own thoughts, controlling the randomness of umbra portals<br /> 3 for Strengthening or weakening bans or wards, making certain processes like Time 4 pause effects not succumb to the effects of Paradox (allowing them to last longer).<br /> 4 for making pattern bleed happen less, or not at all depending on the strength of it all.<br /> 5 for basically becoming the god of circumstance. Added with mind and you can make specific thoughts and ideas just happen. Make specific events in Time or Space go more or less the way you want them to. And oh yeah, basically not have to worry about Spirits getting in your face.<br /> <br /> While the other spheres deal with patterns directly. I like to think of Entropy as dealing with the space around these patterns, the things which govern how they work.<br /> <br /> If you don't like Entropy just because &quot;other spheres can do it&quot; then it could simply be that someone's playing Entropy wrong. It covers a really specific and unique aspect of the game that some of the other spheres may allude to, but none of the other spheres grasp.<br /> <br /> But hey, if you want Entropy to be useless in your game, by all means have it be useless in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T23:40:39-07:00","id":990299,"title":"","content":"Hey, can we get back to talking about sex magick? You know, the purpose behind this thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:30:47-07:00","id":990426,"title":"","content":"I have allowed players to use sex for recovering Mana when they were playing Sorcerers. In addition, I have allowed players to double Chi recovery during consenting sex with adult humans when they were playing Dhampyr (or Shih). I imagine that I would allow an hour of consensual sexual activity with adult humans to count for one point of Quintessence for the purposes of True Magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:41:38-07:00","id":990513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=990299#post990299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, can we get back to talking about sex magick? You know, the purpose behind this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did <i>try</i>....<br /> <br /> I still think sex magic is best represented by using the rules for Rituals and setting up continuous effects... A magical &quot;afterglow&quot;, if you will. Or for rituals that complete effects in situ, as it were. E.g. You could defend your mind for the rest of the day following a session of great sex as an example of &quot;afterglow&quot;. You could look through time one way or the other while having sex as a magical casting that are begun and completed during the act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:12:35-07:00","id":990627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=987945#post987945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address @Maud'Dib, I don't even know if the Time 4 element of that ritual is strictly necessary, though you could still do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm....yes actually it's not needed. :-P I thought that a Cultist fireball rote should totally have Time in it. It can be changed though<br /> <br /> <b>Flames of Love</b> Forces 3 or 5, Time 4, Prime 2 ; possibly Correspondence 2, 3 or 4.<br /> This idea behind this rote is simple - use the passion of sex to power a fireball or firestorm effect. In the case of Forces 3, the focus for this spell is a single cigarette left from a pack smoked during an amorous meeting. (The pack doesn't have to be a full pack - a pack of two cigarettes works just as well, though not for those still learning the rote.) The fireball is contained within the cigarette, and using Prime and Forces sights allows to know how strong the blast will be.<br /> The cigarette can be smoked at any time, the act of which hangs the fireball at the place of the smoking, centered at the point where the butt is dropped. The time until the explosion is determined by the length of smoking the cigarette - so burning through one in 20 seconds will mean the Mage has to get out of there are very quickly, while a normal smoke of 2-3 minutes will give the Mage plenty of time.<br /> (The length of smoking the cigarettes with one's paramour does not matter.)<br /> <br /> In order for this rote work correctly, the Mage can't move more than 3 meters out of the point where he lit the cigarette. The butt must also be dropped - not flicked or thrown - for this rote to work. Trying to drop the butt from a skyscraper or a higher floor causes the rote to fail or botch.<br /> If Correspondence 2 is added, the Mage can move around after lighting the cigarette, as much as he wants; but he must keep smoking and holding the cigarette normally - no hiding of it under the coat or inside a bag! The fireball is hanged at the point where the butt is dropped.<br /> If Correspondence 3 is added, the Mage can move around, and the butt can be flicked - the fireball is hanged on the butt the moment it leaves the Mage's hand. The butt can be flicked from a bridge or into a building through a window etc., and the spell will work.<br /> With Correspondence 4, the Mage can hang the spell so that, by lighting a lighter and whispering his name, the Mage's paramour can alert him to danger to her. This allows him to view the location of his lover, and, if he lights the cigarette in response, creates a co-location of the Mage next to her. This allows him to smoke the cigarette and hang the fireball at the location - hopefully in such a way that protects his lover.<br /> <br /> If the cigarette is smoked by anyone else but the Mage, it is the Mage who suffers the consequences, if any occur. (Sometimes the spell simply dissipates.)<br /> <br /> With Forces 5 and organizing an intricate orgy, a Master of Forces can unleash a firestorm. A minimum of five cigarettes are needed to store the flames; examining them with Forces and Prime sights inform of the spell's potency. The inferno can be shaped by dropping the cigarette butts in various locations - or stacking them all in the same place. After smoking the last cigarette, the Mage can decide when the blaze will occur - but the countdown can be no shorter than the length of the quickest smoking involved, and no longer than the combined time for which all the cigarettes were smoked. The Forces 5 version can be combined with the Correspondence additions.<br /> The persons who took part in the orgy can later help in unleashing the blaze by smoking the cigarettes - even if they are unaware of what they are contributing towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:04:23-07:00","id":990721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=990426#post990426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have allowed players to use sex for recovering Mana when they were playing Sorcerers. In addition, I have allowed players to double Chi recovery during consenting sex with adult humans when they were playing Dhampyr (or Shih). I imagine that I would allow an hour of consensual sexual activity with adult humans to count for one point of Quintessence for the purposes of True Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are very very nice... Quintessence is usually much more dear. A nice steady tantric session could end up being more productive than a human sacrifice, or, honestly, even than small investments in the Node background. That throws risk/reward ratios all out of whack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:28:23-07:00","id":990734,"title":"","content":"Well, I do not let them store the Quintessence that is generated by sex, it has to be spent during a tantric ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T19:36:12-07:00","id":990760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=990721#post990721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are very very nice... Quintessence is usually much more dear. A nice steady tantric session could end up being more productive than a human sacrifice, or, honestly, even than small investments in the Node background. That throws risk/reward ratios all out of whack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how. You can literally convert small amounts of electricity into quint. Meaning anyone with a power hookup has all the quint they could ever practically need. Throw in a forces effect to make perfect solar panels and you might even not have a ludicrously huge electric bill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T00:01:29-07:00","id":990831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=990760#post990760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how. You can literally convert small amounts of electricity into quint. Meaning anyone with a power hookup has all the quint they could ever practically need. Throw in a forces effect to make perfect solar panels and you might even not have a ludicrously huge electric bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true if you have Prime 4 IRC.<br /> And it is debatable if 1 quint equals a small amount of energy when you can create a BIG amount out of 1 quint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:18:59-07:00","id":990970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987592-sex-magick?p=990760#post990760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how. You can literally convert small amounts of electricity into quint. Meaning anyone with a power hookup has all the quint they could ever practically need. Throw in a forces effect to make perfect solar panels and you might even not have a ludicrously huge electric bill.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. <br /> <br /> So, yeah. I stand by what I said. You need to be an Adept of Prime and you need to have LOTS of sex for a prolonged period of time (or black out a significant area or whatever) or you need to be drawing down on something that is deeply meaningful, like say, sacrifice. <br /> <br /> I'd probably allow the whole &quot;have sex and get Quint from it&quot; even without Prime 4, if you are willing, to, say, kill your partner while having sex and have.... hmmm.... Life and/or Mind and Prime 3. Alternatively, perhaps, Primal Utility and an internet sex stable maybe? <br /> <br /> We aren't in 1st E. anymore. The game isn't focused on Quintessence Wars, but Quint (no matter how marginally useful it actually is rules-wise) is still considered to be important and rare and not as easy to get as you seem to be making it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}